lass=\"source-option-letter\">A</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-5-t1-l-q23\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"A\"></span><span>They could not find the right trees in New Zealand.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">B</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-5-t1-l-q23\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"B\"></span><span>They were introduced to other fabrics by the Europeans.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-5-t1-l-q23\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>They found a better material for making fabric.</span></div></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">24</strong> Large pieces of tapa are made from smaller pieces which are</span><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">A</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-5-t1-l-q24\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"A\"></span><span>stuck together.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">B</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-5-t1-l-q24\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"B\"></span><span>woven together.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-5-t1-l-q24\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>sewn together.</span></div></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":4},{"id":"en-practice-source-5-t1-l-g3-1","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"matching_features","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 25-30","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><p>According to the speakers, what function has tapa played in the following countries?</p><p>Write the correct letter, A, B, C or D, next to Questions 25-30.</p></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"matching-dnd-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • Samoa<span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">25</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-5-t1-l-q25\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • Tonga<span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">26</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-5-t1-l-q26\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • Cook Islands<span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">27</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-5-t1-l-q27\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • Fiji<span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">28</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-5-t1-l-q28\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • Tahiti<span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">29</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-5-t1-l-q29\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • Tikopia<span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">30</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-5-t1-l-q30\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div></div><div class=\"options-dnd-panel dnd-panel dnd-panel--matching\"><div class=\"dnd-panel-instruction\">Drag and drop an option to fill in each blank.</div><div class=\"dnd-cards-container\"><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"A\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">A.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">recreational</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"B\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">B.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">practical</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"C\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">C.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">spiritual</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"D\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">D.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">commercial</span></div></div></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":6}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/recent_actual_test_5_academic_listening_test_1_3.mp3"],"order_index":3},{"id":"en-practice-source-5-t1-l-p4","title":"Part 4","part_number":4,"passage_text":"","audio_url":"https://ielts-listening-audio.engnovatemedia.com/3125645-recent_actual_test_5_academic_listening_test_1_4.mp3","question_groups":[{"id":"en-practice-source-5-t1-l-g4-0","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 31-40","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><div class=\"source-section-content-wrapper\"><p>Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER for each answer.</p><p><b>Monarch Butterflies</b></p><p><b>Hibernation</b></p><p>Butterfly species adopt different hibernation patterns during their life cycle.</p><p>Butterflies named 'Banded Hair Freak' hibernate in the form of an <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">31</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-5-t1-l-q31\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></p><p>A species called 'Dapple White' accumulates <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">32</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-5-t1-l-q32\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> from larval stage.</p><p>Slow metabolism can help them to sort out some problems in winter.</p><p>A substance is produced in the blood which may function as <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">33</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-5-t1-l-q33\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></p><p>There are few predators because they can only survive in <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">34</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-5-t1-l-q34\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> weather.</p><p><b>Migration</b></p><p>Monarch butterflies move to <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">35</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-5-t1-l-q35\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> in winter.</p><p>To avoid cold temperature, they migrate to the south in large groups.</p><p>The survival skill can help them last for up to <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">36</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-5-t1-l-q36\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> during a long journey.</p><p>Monarch butterflies fly in the daytime and stay in <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">37</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-5-t1-l-q37\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> during night.</p><p>Researchers found out that they orient by flying along the <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">38</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-5-t1-l-q38\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></p><p>They also follow the direction of the <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">39</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-5-t1-l-q39\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> for navigational aid.</p><p>During migration, they mainly feed on flowers and cannot reproduce.</p><p>Recently the annual arrival of the monarchs can be a good interest to <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">40</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-5-t1-l-q40\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> in the region.</p></div></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-que